<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109992" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕψιστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			Sup.
		 without any Posit. in use: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕψι,
		ὑψοῦ</span>):— <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>highest, loftiest,</i> of places, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				720
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.1026
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τοῖς ὑ.,</span> i. e.
			in heaven above, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				21.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				2.14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of Zeus,
				<i>highest,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				1.60
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				11.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				28
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζηνὸς ὕψιστον σέβας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1289
				</span></i>
			: one of the gates of Thebes was called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὕψισται</span> from his temple there, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				9.8.5
			</span></i>: of Jahweh. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ θεὸς ὁ ὕ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Ge.</u>
					14.18
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>De.</u>
				32.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				96.7
			</span></i> (Egypt, <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1181
			</span></i> (Rhenea, <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>), etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of things, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέφανος, κέρδος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				1.100
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>I.</u>
				1.51
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακῶν ὕψιστα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					331
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				807
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕ. ἐν βροτοῖς φόβος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					479
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
